  "market_context": "Uptrend on AUDUSD 1-hour chart with consecutive higher lows. Price had recently broken structure upward, establishing bullish market structure before the divergence formed.",
  "key_observation": "Price made a higher low while RSI made a lower low (hidden bullish divergence), signaling trend continuation; entry triggered after the divergence candle closed above the trendline.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified an uptrend via consecutive higher lows and drew a yellow upward-sloping trendline connecting swing lows.",
    "Step 2: Added the TMA Divergence Indicator (RSI-based) and enabled only 'hidden bullish divergence' detection.",
    "Step 3: Observed price forming a higher low while RSI formed a lower low — confirming hidden bullish divergence.",
    "Step 4: Waited for the divergence candle to close, then entered long with stop loss below that candle’s low.",
    "Step 5: Set TP1 at the previous S/R level (0.73575–0.73590) and TP2 at the next S/R level, achieving 1:3 R:R and 46 pips profit.",
    "Step 6: Later identified a regular bearish divergence (price higher high, RSI lower high) as the exit signal for the long trade."
  ],
  "outcome": "46 pips profit, 1:3 risk-to-reward ratio; exited on regular bearish divergence at prior S/R level.",
  "lessons": "Hidden divergences in established trends offer high-probability continuation entries. Combine with trendline confluence and precise S/R targets. Use regular divergences as timely exit signals.",
